# Foundry build artefacts. Regenerable with `forge build`.
out/
cache/
broadcast/

# NOTE: lib/ is deliberately NOT ignored. forge-std 1.9.6 is vendored into this
# repository as ordinary tracked files rather than pulled as a git submodule.
#
# Two reasons, and the second is the load-bearing one. First, `git clone` followed by
# `forge test` has to work on the first attempt without a --recursive flag anyone can
# forget. Second, and more important: the 140 tests and every gas figure in DESIGN.md
# are properties of *these exact bytes* compiled by solc 0.8.28 at optimizer_runs = 200,
# and the deployed bytecode at 0x3744E93B9e796E05CB66311d897559B6F3860196 is verified
# on-chain against them. Re-resolving the dependency risks silently fetching a different
# forge-std and invalidating the whole baseline. Vendoring is what makes the build
# reproducible, which for an audited contract matters more than a tidy dependency graph.
#
# Cost of this choice, stated honestly: `forge update` will fight it, and the diff on any
# future forge-std bump will be large. Bump deliberately, in its own commit, and re-run
# the full suite plus `forge test --profile deep` afterwards.

# Node
node_modules/

# Scratch logs from build and test runs, tee'd at the project root for troubleshooting.
# Ignored by default so the repo does not accumulate them. A log gets PROMOTED into
# evidence/ once it proves a published number or records a live-chain observation, and
# evidence/README.md maps every file there to the specific claim it backs.
*.log
!evidence/*.log

# Editors and OS
.DS_Store
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/

# Never commit these. There is no .env in this project and there should never be one:
# both testnet wallets live in Foundry's encrypted keystore under ~/.foundry/keystores,
# outside this tree, and are referenced by account NAME (--account remit-testnet) so no
# key material ever enters a command, a shell history, or a file. Arc's own tutorial uses
# `cast wallet new` with no path plus a plaintext PRIVATE_KEY in .env; this project
# deliberately deviates. The keystore password belongs in a password manager or on paper,
# never in this folder.
.env
*.key
*.keystore
keystore*
*.mnemonic
